# SRT.Core.MessageBroker.RabbitMQ (Cursor rule template)

This file is an **install template**. Copy it to the consumer project’s `.cursor/rules/` and keep the package-prefixed filename:

`SRT.Core.MessageBroker.RabbitMQ.CURSOR_RULE.mdc`

## Mandatory

Before using or modifying this package, follow:

- `docs/SRT.Core.MessageBroker.RabbitMQ.AI_RULES.md` (canonical)
- `docs/SRT.Core.MessageBroker.RabbitMQ.API_REFERENCE.md`
- `docs/SRT.Core.MessageBroker.RabbitMQ.COOKBOOK.md` for host/appsettings

## Working rule

Read docs first. Do not invent APIs. If ambiguous, inspect related code and update the docs.

## Hard constraints (summary)

- Thin host `Program.cs`; no host `UseAuthorization` / `MapControllers`
- Enable via `lstRabbitMQNamespace` + ProjectReference; configure `ConnectionDB:SRTCore_RabbitMQ`
- Add `Service.Id` / `Service.Name` to every environment appsettings file
- Shared `IRabbitConnection`; dispose channels only from publishers/consumers
- Publish success = confirm + no BasicReturn
- Rabbit TLS optional: `UseTls = sslEnabled || caPath`; bad/missing `caPath` fails fast
- Do not copy Redis `tls-auth-clients` into RabbitMQ Docker
- **Initial RabbitMQ setup:** ask human for TLS yes/no and custom CA vs system trust; placeholder `caPath` (e.g. `tls/ca.pem`) if path unknown
